# Model comparisons for the selected exchanged component

The selected-factor interface preserves relative subnormality and the original
setwise product. The actual factor quotient embeds in H/O₂(H), and the local
orbit maps equivariantly into the internal module on representatives and on
the component quotient.

The checked comparisons exclude the alternating degrees six through eight,
the exceptional A₇ and triple-cover A₆ blocks, Sp₄(4), G₂(2)′, and the two
binary-linear groups. A surviving natural L₂ block retains its own even field
exponent and mod-three condition, including the PSL₂(4)/PSL₂(5) overlap.

The complete C.2.7 application, its local radical consequence, the SL₃ model
comparison, and the five C.1.34 module exclusions remain necessary to prove
`SelectedConclusion`. This module does not yet assert that terminal result.
The A₅-block is retained for its independent exclusion owner.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), C.2.7,
C.1.34, and the proof of 15.4.20, printed p.1164.
-/
